	<changelog>
		 * Version 17.1.26 * - Remove unsupported fixed voicemail playback and originate delays; restore native VoiceMailPlayMsg while preserving XML and stale-link fixes
		 * Version 17.1.25 * - Fix visual voicemail replay after message moves to Old, avoid XML parser race and delay audio after auto-answer to prevent cutoff
		 * Version 17.1.24 * - Fix standalone voicemail endpoint bootstrap on FreePBX 17 and automatically republish it after upgrade
		 * Version 17.1.23 * - Visual voicemail Messages menu with per-phone authenticated mailbox lists, auto-answer playback showing voicemail caller ID, mark-heard and delete actions
		 * Version 17.1.22 * - Configurable shared Cisco Directories, Services and Messages menus and optional signed internal phoneServices provisioning
		 * Version 17.1.21 * - Make Cisco directory menu, contact list and Services titles, prompts and entry labels editable in Phone Content without phone reset
		 * Version 17.1.20 * - Publish and sign ringtone catalog as exact lowercase ringlist.xml.sgn requested by Cisco 7945G; automatically republish existing ringtone library
		 * Version 17.1.19 * - Fix Cisco wallpaper signed file header to include the full Desktops path; re-sign files that were incorrectly labeled
		 * Version 17.1.18 * - Sign wallpaper List.xml and image files for ITL-trusted Cisco VPN phones, and ringtones; auto-sign existing media
		 * Version 17.1.17 * - Restore FreePBX-native Phone Content UI; remove duplicate directory entries; automatically publish signed phone config on contact setup and wallpaper upload; report TFTP root mismatches
		 * Version 17.1.16 * - Fix static directory hosting outside AMPWEBROOT, 7945G missing wallpaper commonProfile, and stale Directory URLs; add Phone Content diagnostics and improved UI
		 * Version 17.1.15 * - Add Phone Content tabs (directory, wallpaper, ringtone) with managed Cisco XML, automatic service URLs and upload conversion
		 * Version 17.1.14 * - Fix SCCP phone XML regeneration signing stale TFTP-root XML instead of new settings XML; preserve ITL and show actionable errors
		 * Version 17.1.13 * - Build Cisco SVC-compatible ocserv automatically on Debian 12 and migrate the managed VPN service to the new binary
		 * Version 17.1.12 * - Enable Cisco IP phone /svc compatibility in ocserv VPN configurations (fix failed 7945 VPN login)
		 * Version 17.1.11 * - Manage VPN accounts from the GUI; show connected clients and recent authentication events
		 * Version 17.1.10 * - Keep AMI connected when chan-sccp is absent so a clean installation can bootstrap the driver
		 * Version 17.1.9 * - Bootstrap chan-sccp on first installation from root CLI, including a completely removed driver
		 * Version 17.1.8 * - Streamline VPN and signing UI into Server Config; detect PBX LAN IP and simplify VPN address input
		 * Version 17.1.7 * - Save VPN firewall services and client zone without starting or restarting FreePBX Firewall
		 * Version 17.1.6 * - Manage FreePBX Firewall services for the VPN ports and client pool automatically
		 * Version 17.1.6 * - Install and configure ocserv, VPN TLS certificate, address pool, routes and shared login from SCCP Manager
		 * Version 17.1.6 * - Global defaults plus per-device VPN, signing and endpoint configuration; no MAC allowlist
		 * Version 17.1.6 * - Restore SCCP realtime status parsing, nullable device lookup, and externhost configuration
		 * Version 17.1.6 * - Fix missing AMI realm and malformed address crashes; regression tests added.
		 * Version 17.1.6 * - Development build: managed Cisco VPN profiles, root-owned signing helper, ocserv service controls and per-phone signing
		 * Version 13.0.0.1 * - Alfa Release tested on freepbx v.13.0.192.16, v.14.0.1.5
		 * Version 13.0.0.2 * - Release tested
		 * Version 14.0.0.1 * - Alfa Release new DB structure Add User mobility
		 * Version 14.1.0.1 * - Migrated to chan-sccp repo
		 * Version 14.2.0.1 * - Retired old interface - min chan-sccp v433
		 * Version 14.2.0.2 * - Fix module database definition
		 * Version 14.2.0.5 * - Replace Modals with fpbxToast
		 * Version 14.2.0.8 * - Fix uninstaller and create backup
		 * Version 14.2.0.9 * - Bug Fix - incorrect response class for Reset Token Device
		 * Version 14.2.0.10 * - Bug Fix - line not assigned on device creation
		 * Version 14.3.0.0 * - New Minor Version - Change DB and add new settings
		 * Version 14.3.0.15 * - Get masterFilesList from provisoner via installer Fix Issue 39
		 * Version 14.3.0.16 * - Test version for freepbx upgrader.
		 * Version 14.3.0.17 * - Test version for freepbx upgrader.
		 * Version 14.3.0.18 * - Fix Issue 42
		 * Version 14.3.0.22 * - Fix Issue 50
		 * Version 14.3.0.23 * - Fix Issue 49
		 * Version 14.3.0.25 * - Fix Issue 55
		 * Version 14.3.0.26 * - Fix Issue 54
		 * Version 14.3.0.27 * - Standardise treatment of SIP and SCCP hardware.
		 * Version 14.3.0.28 * - Fix issue with RNav which caused exception with new device
		 * Version 14.3.0.29 * - Fix issue reloading page after saving settings and not restarting devices.
		 * Version 14.3.0.30 * - Fix reversion in 29. Not returning to correct page when saving device.
		 * Version 14.3.0.31 * - Fix rewrite rules.
		 * Version 14.4.0.1 * - Modify installer to avoid data loss on existing 14.3 fields. Bump Minor version to reflect this.
		 * Version 14.4.0.2 * - Revert error in Installer db calls - IF EXISTS is not valid in MariaDb v5 (package DB)
		 * Version 14.4.0.3 * - Change method of selecting phonecodepage depending on if is java phone.
		 * Version 14.4.0.5 * - Fix issue #59.
		 * Version 14.5.0.2 * - Fix issue #32.
		 * Version 14.5.0.4 * - Fix issue where values with spaces are truncated. Preserve softkeys accross installs
		 * Version 15.0.1 * - Own fork, Asterisk 20 / FreePBX 16 support
		 * Version 17.0.1 * - Adapted for Asterisk 23 / FreePBX 17
		 * Version 17.1.0 * - Security and correctness review applied throughout; settings that were saved but never used now take effect (regcontext, pickupgroup, directed pickup, provisioner download switch, explicit CallManager list); phone credentials no longer shipped in templates; useRedialMenu on by default; bundles chan-sccp 4.4.0
		 * Version 17.1.1 * - Bundles chan-sccp 4.4.1; the driver installer's source build uses a plain ./configure; releases are created by CI from a pushed tag
	</changelog>
